    {
      "repo": "PocketDoom",
      "area": "Memory map and loading",
      "facts": [
        "Linker puts 64 KB BRAM at 0x00000000 and Doom firmware at 0x10200000 in SDRAM, with 64 MB SDRAM base 0x10000000.",
        "data.json defines deferred WAD/binary/config inputs and automatic nonvolatile save/config slots in bridge CRAM1 at 0x30000000 and 0x30060000.",
        "Dataslot firmware issues APF open/read/write commands, converts CPU SDRAM 0x10000000 to bridge 0x00000000 and exposes uncached SDRAM alias 0x50000000.",
        "A 512 KB bounce buffer at 0x10180000 and uncached reads are used to avoid stale CPU cache following bridge writes."
      ],
      "reuse": "Deferred loading of user-supplied disk images or extracted data, save persistence, terminal diagnostics, and explicit DMA coherency. Change all data formats/maps for Lotus.",
