      "repo": "PocketDoom",
      "area": "Video/controls",
      "facts": [
        "The compiled scanout reads 320 eight-bit palette indices per line from SDRAM using 32-bit bursts and a 256-entry RGB888 palette.",
        "Firmware renders directly to one SDRAM buffer, evicts cache lines, requests a vsync swap and waits for the pending swap before beginning another frame.",
        "Controller keys/axes/triggers are mapped into system MMIO and software translates edges into engine input."
      ],
      "reuse": "Palette framebuffer and vsync swap are good native-port or software-emulator presentation primitives. Target timing/aspect/line changes must match the actual Lotus platform, especially PAL 50 Hz rather than blindly adopting 60 Hz.",
