    {
      "repo": "PocketQuake",
      "area": "PSRAM code split and accelerators",
      "facts": [
        "Actual linker allocates 32 KB BRAM, 16 MB read-only executable PSRAM at 0x30000000, and SDRAM data/BSS/heap from 0x10400000.",
        "Bootloader loads quake.bin into SDRAM then copies code to PSRAM; initialized writable data remains in SDRAM.",
        "Quake framebuffer uses the uncached SDRAM alias.",
        "HDL contains DMA fill/copy, textured span and z-span rasterizer, SRAM z-buffer fill, and alias transform MAC; these are wired into active core_top."
      ],
      "reuse": "PSRAM execution can separate instruction traffic from data/framebuffer traffic, at cost of controller/CDC/timing complexity. DMA fill/copy is general; remaining acceleration is specialized.",
